abstract: >-
  A 2D azimuth-based simulation of blind human echolocation
  using a Kalman filter. Simulates test and control
  conditions from [Patel VSS 2024; Teng & Fusco, 2026],
  aiming to model how information is accumulated across
  echolocation clicks to estimate a target location. The
  computational model integrates Bayesian belief estimation
  using a Kalman filter (KF), binaural audio processing, and
  motor control to simulate how people localize targets
  using self-generated click sounds. The KF continuously
  updates a belief estimate of target location from
  echo-derived ITD measurements, with movement bias scaling
  proportionally to KF confidence.
keywords:
  - echolocation
